  {
   "text": "I registered Samuel Okonkwo as a new patient (patient ID 4) with the values you gave, and the dashboard now shows DOB 1979-03-08.\n\n- **DOB:** it was saved as 1979-08-03 the first time, so I corrected it in the edit form. The patient banner at the top of the dashboard still showed the old date and age after the save, but the Demographics section shows 1979-03-08.\n- **Sex:** I set both \"Birth Sex\" and \"Sex\" to Male. Birth Sex is a required field and the task only said \"sex\", so I used Male for both.\n- **Email:** I put it in \"Contact Email\" and left \"Trusted Email\" blank.\n- **Address:** the app displays the street and city in capitals (7 CEDAR LANE, SPRINGFIELD).\n- **External ID:** the system filled this in as 4 on its own, and I left it alone.\n- **Popup:** I dismissed the OpenEMR product registration popup with \"Ask again later\" so I could get to the patient form.\n\nThe duplicate check found no existing patient before I created the record.\n\nRESULT: DONE patient ID 4 (Samuel Okonkwo)",
